WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:04.670
Paying off virtually everything that was set
up in the last 11 years of the Marvel Cinematic

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:09.870
Universe, Avengers: Endgame truly feels like
the culmination of the 21 films that preceded

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:10.870
it.

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:14.070
The filmmaking team achieves this by tying
up tiny stories, calling back movies they

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:17.630
released years ago, and confirming lots of
fan theories.

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:21.880
And then Marvel execs took it one step further
by including basically everyone who's ever

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:25.699
starred in an MCU movie and giving them a
role in Endgame.

00:00:25.699 --> 00:00:29.850
Case in point: That mysterious kid at the
end of the film that everyone is bending over

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:31.380
backwards to remember.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:34.640
Warning: We're now entering spoiler county!

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:39.620
After the Avengers faced off against Thanos
and won, they assembled once more for a heartbreaking

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:44.530
reason: to attend the funeral of Tony Stark,
who sacrificed himself by snatching the Infinity

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:48.720
Stones away from the purple-faced despot,
then snapping his own fingers in order to

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:52.030
blast Thanos and his alien minions into oblivion.

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:56.970
The funeral scene begins with the heroes gathered
around Tony's beloved Pepper Potts and watching

00:00:56.970 --> 00:01:01.500
a hologram message Tony recorded the day before
the Avengers traveled back in time to collect

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:02.850
the Stones.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:07.429
It ends with a solemn sweeping shot of Tony's
closest friends watching his original arc

00:01:07.429 --> 00:01:09.810
reactor float across the lake.

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:13.700
But a genuine pop-culture mystery has arisen
from all this melancholy:

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:15.420
"Freeze!

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:18.880
Don't move."

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:20.490
"You got me."

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:25.259
Audience members are having a hard time remembering
the brunette-haired teenage boy standing completely

00:01:25.259 --> 00:01:26.770
alone at the funeral.

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:29.280
Who is he and how did he know Tony?

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:33.469
We have the answer for you: The character
was just a precocious young boy when he last

00:01:33.469 --> 00:01:37.859
popped up in the Marvel Cinematic Universe…
way back in Iron Man 3.

00:01:37.859 --> 00:01:41.099
He's Harley Keener, portrayed by actor Ty
Simpkins.

00:01:41.099 --> 00:01:45.709
You may also recognize the actor from his
2015 appearance in Jurassic World.

00:01:45.709 --> 00:01:50.249
If you can't recall, here's how Harley and
Tony first met: Searching for food, shelter,

00:01:50.249 --> 00:01:55.329
and a place to recharge his suit, Tony breaks
into the garage of Harley's home in Rose Hill,

00:01:55.329 --> 00:01:56.329
Tennessee.

00:01:56.329 --> 00:02:00.170
The two characters form an unlikely but incredibly
sweet bond in the film.

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:04.560
Throughout his friendship with Harley, Tony
softens and reveals his fatherly side — a

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:08.679
side we also saw when he mentored Peter Parker
in Spider-Man: Homecoming.

00:02:08.679 --> 00:02:13.879
When Iron Man 3 opened in theaters in 2013,
Simpkins was just 11 years old.

00:02:13.879 --> 00:02:19.329
Now, he's 17, which explains why he looks
virtually unrecognizable in Avengers: Endgame.

00:02:19.329 --> 00:02:23.019
Those who keep a finger on the pulse of all
things Marvel might not have been entirely

00:02:23.019 --> 00:02:27.280
shocked to see Harley Keener make an appearance
in the film: Simpkins' casting was confirmed

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:30.360
way back in October of 2017.

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:34.129
Simpkins' physical appearance came as a bit
of a surprise though, since he's now a teenager

00:02:34.129 --> 00:02:38.689
and not the tiny lad in Iron Man 3, but it
was never a secret that he was going figure

00:02:38.689 --> 00:02:40.430
into Avengers: Endgame somehow

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:44.939
When news of Simpkins joining Avengers: Endgame
went public, fans wondered if Harley would

00:02:44.939 --> 00:02:46.769
play a substantial role in the movie.

00:02:46.769 --> 00:02:50.890
After Spider-Man disintegrated in Avengers:
Infinity War, some folks wondered if Keener

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:54.409
would step into his shoes and become Tony's
latest protege.

00:02:54.409 --> 00:02:58.379
But others hit the nail on the head and predicted
exactly what ended up happening: Harley was

00:02:58.379 --> 00:03:04.019
also a victim of the Decimation, and his involvement
in Endgame consisted solely of a brief, somewhat

00:03:04.019 --> 00:03:05.659
confusing cameo.

00:03:05.659 --> 00:03:09.719
Maybe he only had a few seconds of screen
time and no lines to deliver, but Harley's

00:03:09.719 --> 00:03:13.140
appearance at Tony's funeral still made quite
an impact.

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:18.319
The MCU began with Iron Man over a decade
ago in 2008, and with the character's passing

00:03:18.319 --> 00:03:23.050
in Avengers: Endgame, the superhero franchise
as we know it has come to an end.

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:27.489
It only makes sense that everyone who admired
Tony would attend his funeral to say goodbye…

00:03:27.489 --> 00:03:30.469
even the young boy he met all those years
ago.

00:03:30.469 --> 00:03:34.549
As much as Tony tried to resist friendship
and intimacy earlier in his life, he was clearly

00:03:34.549 --> 00:03:36.140
loved by many.

